{
 "note": "Mutants of the network handicap of a room's computer players (docs/BOTS.md, 'The network handicap of a room's bots'): the hold's rounding, cap, median, the band and the dwell that keep it from flickering, nobody connected and nobody readable, the order of the held commands, the pass-through at a hold of 0, the turn that applied_at names, the sink that waits for a match that waits, the host's reading of a person's turns (the readings it needs, how old one may be, the cap of a reading, a turn it has not run, a turn twice), the calls that feed the reading, and the room's use of it, against test_server S3.285 - S3.290 and test_latency N9.40 - N9.44. Run from the checkout with a configured build folder: python3 tools/mutate.py tests/data/bot_lag_mutants.json --keep-going --jobs 1 --timeout 900. Every mutant must be caught by the case named in expect. Left out as equivalent: the cap of bot_lag_ticks_for without its early return's twin (std::min alone gives the same number for every reading that does not wrap, which the overflow mutant covers), and the clamp of BotLag::update's median (a median past 600 ms gives the cap with or without it, except at the wrap of the sum, which the huge reading covers).",
 "baseline": [
  {
   "build": "test_server",
   "test": "timeout 900 env ANTS_TEST_FILTER='S3.28' ./build/tests/test_server/test_server"
  },
  {
   "build": "test_latency",
   "test": "timeout 900 env ./build/tests/test_net/test_latency"
  }
 ],
